<title>THAILAND: Thai April sugar exports drop to 465,213 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai April sugar exports drop to 465,213 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai sugar exports fell sharply to 465,213 tonnes in April from 661,255 tonnes in the same month last year and 776,405 tonnes in March, an independent surveyor said on Monday.</p>
<p>Of the total, 295,475 tonnes were raw sugar, 80,988 tonnes white and 88,750 tonnes brown, the surveyor said.</p>
<p>The country exported 2.14 million tonnes during the first four months of 1997 versus around 2.73 million tonnes during the corresponding period last year.</p>
<p>Indonesia was the biggest buyer in April, importing 140,369 tonnes of sugar, mostly white. Other major buyers included Japan and Malaysia who bought around 70,930 tonnes and 67,550 tonnes respectively.</p>
<p>China bought only 14,200 tonnes during the same month.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsrom (662) 652-0642</p>
